{"title":"Career Roadmap · Geotechnical Analyst","role":"Geotechnical Analyst","summary":"A Geotechnical Analyst studies soil, rock, groundwater and subsurface conditions to support the safe and economical design of foundations, slopes, tunnels, roads, dams, retaining structures, mines and other infrastructure.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. Geology / Earth Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["The role combines geology","soil/rock mechanics","field investigation","laboratory testing","GIS","geotechnical data analysis."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Career reality","text":"A B.Sc. in Geology can provide entry-level opportunities in geological investigation, site investigation and geotechnical support. However, specialised design responsibility and progression toward professional geotechnical engineering roles often require an M.Sc./M.Tech./M.E. or other relevant postgraduate qualification, depending on the employer and role."},{"type":"note","label":"Typical pathway","text":"B.Sc. Geology → Field/Geotechnical Internship → Site Investigation Trainee → Geotechnical Analyst → Senior Analyst → Geotechnical Specialist → Project/Technical Lead"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Geology, mineralogy, soil, rock and field fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Engineering geology, soil/rock classification and field investigation"}],[{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"Geotechnical testing + GIS + site investigation internship"}],[{"text":"2029–2030"},{"text":"Geotechnical Analyst / Geological Site Investigation role"}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Subsurface investigation and geotechnical data analysis"}],[{"text":"2034–2038"},{"text":"Senior Geotechnical Analyst / Engineering Geologist"}],[{"text":"2038–2042"},{"text":"Geotechnical Specialist / Technical Lead"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Principal Specialist / Project Lead / Geotechnical Consultant"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Earth-science foundation"},{"text":"Geology, mineralogy, physics, mathematics"},{"text":"Geological field notebook"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Engineering geology"},{"text":"Soil, rock, structural geology, groundwater"},{"text":"Site investigation project"}],[{"text":"3rd Year"},{"text":"Geotechnical analysis"},{"text":"Soil testing, rock mechanics, GIS, data analysis"},{"text":"Geotechnical internship"}],[{"text":"4th Year / Advanced"},{"text":"Professional capability"},{"text":"Slope/foundation concepts, modelling, reporting"},{"text":"Major project + field experience"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Build the Earth-Science Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core geology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical geology"},{"text":"Mineralogy"},{"text":"Petrology"},{"text":"Structural geology"},{"text":"Geomorphology"},{"text":"Stratigraphy"},{"text":"Sedimentology"},{"text":"Hydrology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand geological materials"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Igneous rocks"},{"text":"Sedimentary rocks"},{"text":"Metamorphic rocks"},{"text":"Minerals"},{"text":"Weathered rock"},{"text":"Soil profiles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic engineering knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Field skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Start maintaining a geological field notebook containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Location"},{"text":"Rock type"},{"text":"Soil type"},{"text":"Geological structures"},{"text":"Photographs"},{"text":"Measurements"},{"text":"Field observations"},{"text":"Interpretations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Engineering Geology"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from pure geology toward engineering applications."},{"type":"h","text":"Soil fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Soil formation"},{"text":"Grain-size distribution"},{"text":"Soil classification"},{"text":"Plasticity"},{"text":"Density"},{"text":"Porosity"},{"text":"Permeability"},{"text":"Compaction"},{"text":"Consolidation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rock mechanics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rock strength"},{"text":"Discontinuities"},{"text":"Joints"},{"text":"Faults"},{"text":"Rock mass classification"},{"text":"Weathering"},{"text":"Rock quality"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering geology"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geological hazards"},{"text":"Landslides"},{"text":"Rockfalls"},{"text":"Groundwater"},{"text":"Settlement"},{"text":"Foundation conditions"},{"text":"Excavation stability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Geotechnical Investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student should become comfortable with actual site-investigation workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"Site investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Desk Study","Geological Mapping","Site Reconnaissance","Boreholes/Investigation","Sampling","Laboratory Testing","Data Interpretation","Geotechnical Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Boreholes"},{"text":"Trial pits"},{"text":"Soil sampling"},{"text":"Rock coring"},{"text":"Groundwater observations"},{"text":"SPT"},{"text":"CPT concepts"},{"text":"Geophysical investigation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Moisture content"},{"text":"Grain-size analysis"},{"text":"Atterberg limits"},{"text":"Specific gravity"},{"text":"Compaction"},{"text":"Permeability"},{"text":"Shear strength"},{"text":"Consolidation"},{"text":"Unconfined compression"},{"text":"Rock strength testing"}]}]},{"heading":"Geotechnical Data Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Geotechnical Analyst must turn raw investigation data into useful engineering information."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Borehole logs"},{"text":"SPT results"},{"text":"CPT data"},{"text":"Soil classification"},{"text":"Groundwater levels"},{"text":"Rock core data"},{"text":"Laboratory results"},{"text":"Geological profiles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Produce"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Borehole logs"},{"text":"Geological sections"},{"text":"Soil profiles"},{"text":"Rock-mass descriptions"},{"text":"Site-condition summaries"},{"text":"Geotechnical data tables"}]}]},{"heading":"GIS & Digital Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"GIS is highly valuable for a geology graduate."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"ArcGIS or equivalent"},{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Topographic maps"},{"text":"Geological maps"},{"text":"Digital elevation models"},{"text":"Spatial analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Use GIS for"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geological mapping"},{"text":"Landslide susceptibility"},{"text":"Site selection"},{"text":"Terrain analysis"},{"text":"Groundwater studies"},{"text":"Infrastructure corridors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Python can help automate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Borehole-data processing"},{"text":"Laboratory-data analysis"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Plotting"},{"text":"Geotechnical datasets"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Choose a Specialisation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type"